{"title":"1962 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A regular dodecagon (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sides) is inscribed in a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> inches. The area of the dodecagon, in square inches, is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23e518ddcda919e93322cec6c24d2bec4042b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3r^2 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2r^2 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3r^2\\sqrt{3}/4 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ r^2\\sqrt{3} \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3r^2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"514\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for the area of a regular dodecagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d9543d9bb94c0194aa106d2852f40d056bb686fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3r^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n(If you don't know this formula, it's pretty easy to figure out that the area of a square inscribed in a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdc3bd06d3f13fde4505d5bf487f683e24ad96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, and all the choices except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d9543d9bb94c0194aa106d2852f40d056bb686fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3r^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdc3bd06d3f13fde4505d5bf487f683e24ad96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />. Remember, the more sides a regular polygon has, the closer its area gets to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e89ed1c5456915b4e95e0c8a11257ac5ed3d32c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME\" title=\"1962 AHSME\">1962 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1962 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1962 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1962\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"cente